From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: slothfulchat <patches@slothfulchat.invalid>
Date: Mon, 6 Jul 2026 22:34:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wasm: read the JS clock everywhere std::time panics

std::time::{SystemTime,Instant}::now() abort on wasm32-unknown-unknown.
- rustls: JsClockTimeProvider via ClientConfig::builder_with_details
  (cert validation calls UnixTime::now during the handshake)
- tools: time_now() returns a wasm-safe Instant; Time::now call sites
  switched; path_is_dir/path_is_file sync-fs helpers for wasm
- deltachat-ratelimit: SystemTime::now via deltachat_time
- jsonrpc: MuteDuration::Until via tools::SystemTime (muting a chat
  for a while panicked the core worker)

Since v2.64.0 upstream builds the rustls config with
ClientConfig::builder() (ring as process default) and lists
deltachat-time as a dev-dependency only; the wasm branch now uses
builder_with_details() with ring plus the JS clock inline, and
deltachat-time is a wasm32 dependency again.
